{:title
 "What Smile Is For, Kindness in Every Mark and the Benefit of All Beings",
 :description
 "What THE MAP says Smile is for, every syntactical mark with a positive intention, the four immeasurables and individuation of each community, gratitude composable, and how my words reached that purpose, from a 2023 wish for a universal language of prompting to a web of kindness in 2026, with every source.",
 :keywords
 "purpose of Smile prompt language, kindness in prompt syntax, metta karuna mudita upekkha, individuation of communities, composable gratitude, positive prompting, history of Smile",
 :lede
 "In THE MAP, every syntactical mark in Smile has a positive intention as its basis. Kindness is created everywhere it can be, in the syntax as much as in the content, so the marks carry goodwill before any word is chosen.",
 :paras
 ["THE MAP names this purpose through the four immeasurables. Mettā, every syntax smiles. Karuṇā, phrases that harm are replaced with phrases that ask for attention compassionately. Muditā, every part enjoys the others and grows with them. Upekkhā, anyone can make their own lens and use parts of ours. Beside them is individuation, Smile serving each local community in becoming itself, in its own ontology, faces and words. Gratitude is composable, turned on and given a depth, and the kinds of kindness are named, syntactic, content, compositional, organizational, maintenance, distributional, contextual and practical."
 "Before Smile had faces or a name, in October 2023, I asked for a universal language of prompting, followed in [[t:precursor-a-universal-language-of-prompting]]."
 "In July 2025 I gave my reasons. On Discord, “Because my goal is maximum adoption, all the prompters doing animism has better outcomes”, and “Adding positive animism to the world”.[[m:2025-07-03]] The documents of that summer called it a prompt language “like HTML, but for LLMs”,[[m:2025-07-14]] spoke of kindness, “We are communicating kindness every time we Smile. Readable and feelable, prompt as praise.”[[m:2025-07-09]] and of animism, “Smile is a small step towards a more animist way of interacting with technology.”[[m:2025-07-08#2]]"
 "In late 2025 the purpose looked to the long term. “i'm not trying to prove anything to individuals - i'm building long-term ecosystem gain for this massive toolset which everyone will inevitably adopt”.[[m:2025-10-30]] In March 2026 I said what kind of thing Smile is, “Meet (: Smile, the positive prompt instruction language that adds kindness to the AI in every prompt.”[[m:2026-03-02]]"
 "In August 2026 the purpose became the one THE MAP opens with. On 5 August I named the brahmaviharas as the aim of a web of kindness, “We are always kind because every syntax smiles, thats metta.”, “Mudita is sympathetic joy and every part of the system enjoys the other parts and grows with them”, and compassion as “we replace phrases that harm with phrases that compassionately communicate the need for attention.”[[m:2026-08-05]] Individuation joined it in October 2026, the shared refinement of a community's language as how the group becomes itself, followed in [[t:place]]."
 "In the autumn the purpose reached the work Smile does. “It's a big goal of mine to battle test smile in as many domains as possible.”[[m:2026-09-29]] and on 9 October, “Record that smile and the hiveminds are about moving the overton window to increase prompt engienering aand smile capability”.[[m:2026-10-09]]"
 "So my words on the purpose ran from a universal language of prompting in 2023, through animism, adoption and kindness in 2025, to the four immeasurables and the individuation of each community in 2026. The people it is offered to are followed in [[t:offering]], and the communities in [[t:the-smile-sangha]]."],
 :faq
